course: dictionary
lesson: 7710
title: The science of the mind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Psychology is a science. It studies the mind, feelings and how people and animals think and behave. You will meet it in lessons about feelings, the body, learning and memory. The ending -ology means "the study of", so psychology is the study of the mind.
explain: Psychology also has a second meaning. Someone's psychology is the way they think and feel, so two people can have very different psychologies even when they are in the same place.
explain: You can use the word in phrases such as study psychology, child psychology or the psychology of colour. A psychologist is a person who works in psychology and helps people with their thoughts and feelings. «Words with silent first letters are found under their real spelling: psychology under ps, knee under kn.» So the silent p tells you where to look in a dictionary.
fact: Psychology is the science that studies the mind, feelings and behaviour.
fact: Psychology has a silent p at the start, so it is found under ps in a dictionary.
fact: A psychologist is a person who studies or works in psychology.
fact: Someone's psychology is the way they think and feel.
fact: Psychology can help explain learning, memory and emotions.
exercise: What does psychology mean? | A type of sport played in schools | The study of stars and planets | *The science that studies the mind, feelings and behaviour | The way a crowd moves
exercise: Where would you look up psychology in a dictionary? | *under ps | under ch | under gy | under sy
exercise: The way a person thinks and feels is their | machine | *psychology | sandwich | sky
test: A psychologist is someone who | bakes bread for a living | repairs cars | *studies the mind and behaviour
test: Which phrase uses psychology correctly? | *the psychology of colour | a pair of socks | the sound of rain
exam: Why is psychology found under ps? | Because it is a fruit that grows on trees | Because all long words start with ps | *Because it starts with a silent p, so you look under its real spelling | Because it has the same spelling as a sport
